[00:00.00] I've tried, I've tried to run and hide, and find a life that's new.
[00:21.00] But where I go, I'll always know that I can't escape from you.
[00:34.00] A jug of wine to numb my mind, but what good does it do?
[00:48.00] A jug runs dry, and still I cry, but I can't escape from you.
[01:18.00] These wasted tears are souvenir of dreams that can't come true.
[01:42.00] But your memory is chained to me, Lord, I can't escape from you.
[01:55.00] I can't pretend this is the end, or dreams cannot come true.
[02:09.00] A slave to long, to a heart of stone, Lord, I can't escape from you.
